# Rotas da API - rode na ordem, com o backend no ar (./mvnw spring-boot:run).
# O banco H2 começa vazio a cada inicialização: o aluno criado abaixo recebe id 1
# e o professor recebe id 2.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

# =====================================================================
# ALUNO (/student)
# =====================================================================

### 1. Criar aluno (espera 201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/student
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Ana Souza",
  "phoneNumber": "(41) 99999-1234",
  "emailAddress": "ana@email.com",
  "status": "ACTIVE",
  "studentNumber": 2024001,
  "addresses": [
    {
      "street": "Rua A, 10",
      "city": "Curitiba",
      "state": "PR",
      "zipCode": "80000-000",
      "country": "Brasil"
    }
  ]
}

### 2. Listar alunos (espera 200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/student

### 3. Buscar aluno por id (espera 200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/student/1

### 4. Editar aluno - manda TODOS os campos (espera 200)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/student/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Ana Souza Lima",
  "phoneNumber": "(41) 98888-0000",
  "emailAddress": "ana.lima@email.com",
  "status": "DISABLE",
  "studentNumber": 2024001,
  "addresses": [
    {
      "street": "Rua A, 10",
      "city": "Curitiba",
      "state": "PR",
      "zipCode": "80000-000",
      "country": "Brasil"
    },
    {
      "street": "Rua B, 20",
      "city": "Joinville",
      "state": "SC",
      "zipCode": "89200-000",
      "country": "Brasil"
    }
  ]
}

# =====================================================================
# PROFESSOR (/professor)
# =====================================================================

### 5. Criar professor (espera 201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/professor
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Carla Mendes",
  "phoneNumber": "(41) 3333-4444",
  "emailAddress": "carla@email.com",
  "status": "ACTIVE",
  "salary": 8500.50,
  "addresses": [
    {
      "street": "Av. Brasil, 500",
      "city": "Curitiba",
      "state": "PR",
      "zipCode": "80010-000",
      "country": "Brasil"
    }
  ]
}

### 6. Listar professores (espera 200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/professor

### 7. Buscar professor por id (espera 200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/professor/2

### 8. Editar professor - aumento de salário (espera 200)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/professor/2
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Carla Mendes",
  "phoneNumber": "(41) 3333-4444",
  "emailAddress": "carla@email.com",
  "status": "ACTIVE",
  "salary": 9500.00,
  "addresses": [
    {
      "street": "Av. Brasil, 500",
      "city": "Curitiba",
      "state": "PR",
      "zipCode": "80010-000",
      "country": "Brasil"
    }
  ]
}

# =====================================================================
# PESSOA (/person) - alunos e professores juntos
# =====================================================================

### 9. Listar todas as pessoas (espera 200, com "type" em cada uma)
GET {{baseUrl}}/person

### 10. Buscar pessoa por id - aqui o 2 é a professora (espera 200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/person/2

# =====================================================================
# ERROS - 404 (id não existe)
# =====================================================================

### 11. Buscar aluno que não existe (espera 404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/student/999

### 12. Buscar como aluno um id que é de professor (espera 404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/student/2

### 13. Editar professor que não existe (espera 404)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/professor/999
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Ninguém",
  "phoneNumber": "(41) 0000-0000",
  "emailAddress": "ninguem@email.com",
  "status": "ACTIVE",
  "salary": 1000.00,
  "addresses": [
    {
      "street": "Rua X",
      "city": "Curitiba",
      "state": "PR",
      "zipCode": "80000-000",
      "country": "Brasil"
    }
  ]
}

### 14. Apagar aluno que não existe (espera 404)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/student/999

# =====================================================================
# ERROS - 400 (dados inválidos)
# =====================================================================

### 15. Criar aluno sem nada (espera 400 com todos os campos obrigatórios)
POST {{baseUrl}}/student
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 16. E-mail inválido e sem endereço (espera 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/student
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Bruno Lima",
  "phoneNumber": "(41) 97777-1111",
  "emailAddress": "email-invalido",
  "status": "ACTIVE",
  "studentNumber": 2024002,
  "addresses": []
}

### 17. Endereço incompleto, sem cidade (espera 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/student
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Bruno Lima",
  "phoneNumber": "(41) 97777-1111",
  "emailAddress": "bruno@email.com",
  "status": "ACTIVE",
  "studentNumber": 2024002,
  "addresses": [
    {
      "street": "Rua C, 30",
      "state": "PR",
      "zipCode": "80000-000",
      "country": "Brasil"
    }
  ]
}

### 18. Professor com salário negativo (espera 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/professor
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Pedro Alves",
  "phoneNumber": "(41) 96666-2222",
  "emailAddress": "pedro@email.com",
  "status": "ACTIVE",
  "salary": -100,
  "addresses": [
    {
      "street": "Rua D, 40",
      "city": "Curitiba",
      "state": "PR",
      "zipCode": "80000-000",
      "country": "Brasil"
    }
  ]
}

### 19. Status que não existe no enum (espera 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/student
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Bruno Lima",
  "phoneNumber": "(41) 97777-1111",
  "emailAddress": "bruno@email.com",
  "status": "PAUSADO",
  "studentNumber": 2024002,
  "addresses": [
    {
      "street": "Rua C, 30",
      "city": "Curitiba",
      "state": "PR",
      "zipCode": "80000-000",
      "country": "Brasil"
    }
  ]
}

# =====================================================================
# APAGAR (por último, para não atrapalhar os testes acima)
# =====================================================================

### 20. Apagar aluno - os endereços dele vão junto (espera 204)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/student/1

### 21. Apagar professor (espera 204)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/professor/2

### 22. Listar de novo - deve voltar vazio (espera 200 com [])
GET {{baseUrl}}/person
